> Original fatal error: **concurrent map read and map write**

----
Which map does the map here refer to?

https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/apis/audit/types.go#L140

```golang
// Event captures all the information that can be included in an API audit log.
type Event struct {
     ....
     // Annotations is an unstructured key value map stored with an audit event that may be set by
     // plugins invoked in the request serving chain, including authentication, authorization and
     // admission plugins. Note that these annotations are for the audit event, and do not correspond
     // to the metadata.annotations of the submitted object. Keys should uniquely identify the informing
     // component to avoid name collisions (e.g. podsecuritypolicy.admission.k8s.io/policy). Values
     // should be short. Annotations are included in the Metadata level.
     // +optional
     Annotations map[string]string
}
```

> Our Audit module uses a Backend that carries a buffer. Then it writes the Audit Log asynchronously [or calls Webhook].

- event.Annotations in the buffer are modified by other goroutines
- The event in the buffer has reached the conditions that need to be output (the Timer deadline has expired, or the Batch Size has been reached), and Encode will be required during the output to the target [File or Socket] 【**no lock operation is performed here ！**】

If the above two conditions are met, we will encounter this error.

----

OK, the core question we are concerned about focuses on when were event.Annotaions written?

- If we fail to call Webhook, the annotations of audit.Event will be written. https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/4a9b9028153c6984b9cf69067cc0a1aa12a00e73/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/webhook/mutating/dispatcher.go#L182
- During the calling process of mutating webhooks, if the webhook generates a patch to the Object, we will store this part of the information in the annotations of the Event. https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/webhook/mutating/dispatcher.go#L455



----

At this point I think the issue is clear. Please correct me if I'm wrong ~

> > #120692
> 
> kubernetes version v1.28.3

Or we may have a minimal fix

```
//staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/audit/context.go
func DeepcopyAuditContextEvent(ac *AuditContext) *auditinternal.Event {
 	ac.annotationMutex.Lock()
 	defer ac.annotationMutex.Unlock()
 
 	return ac.Event.DeepCopy()
 }

```

